      if (trait === shuffledDescriptions[shuffledTraits.indexOf(trait)]) {
        score++;
        scoreDisplay.innerText = `Score: ${score}`;
        // Check if all traits have been matched
        if (score === traits.length) {
          alert("Congratulations! You solved the puzzle!");
        }
      }
    });
    traitsContainer.appendChild(traitButton);
  });
  // Display shuffled descriptions
  shuffledDescriptions.forEach(description => {
    const descriptionButton = document.createElement("button");
    descriptionButton.innerText = description;
    descriptionsContainer.appendChild(descriptionButton);
  });
  // Set up timer
  const countdown = setInterval(() => {
    timer--;
    timerDisplay.innerText = `Time left: ${timer}s`;
    if (timer === 0) {
      clearInterval(countdown);
      alert("Time's up! Game over.");
    }
  }, 1000);
}
```
This code assumes that the API returns an object with two arrays: `traits` and `descriptions`, where each index in `traits` corresponds to the same index in `descriptions`. The code shuffles both arrays and displays them as buttons in separate containers on the webpage. When the user clicks on a trait button, the code checks if its corresponding description matches the description in the shuffled `descriptions` array. If it's a match, the score increases and the trait and description buttons disappear. If the score reaches the length of the `traits` array, the user wins the game. The code also includes a timer that starts at 60 seconds and counts down to 0. If the timer reaches 0, the game ends.

