Here's an updated version of the code that checks if the equation is valid and uses `preg_match()` to only allow numbers and basic arithmetic operators (+, -, *, /):
```
$equation = "6*7"; // or any equation that equals 42
$pattern = "/^[\d+\-*/\s]+$/"; // only allow digits and basic operators
if (!preg_match($pattern, $equation)) {
    echo "Invalid equation";
    exit;
}
$evaluated = eval("return $equation;");
if ($evaluated !== 42) {
    echo "Equation does not equal 42";
    exit;
}
