</html>
```
In this example, we use PouchDB, a JavaScript database that can sync with other databases, to connect to a distributed database running on localhost. We then perform CRUD (create, read, update, delete) operations on the database to demonstrate its advantages. Because the database is distributed, it can be accessed and updated from multiple locations, providing improved scalability, increased availability, and better fault tolerance.

