Can you provide a detailed explanation of code refactoring using Java code as an example?
Consider the following Java code:
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello, World!");
    }
}
What changes can be made to this code to improve its readability and maintainability through refactoring techniques? Can you explain the process of refactoring and its benefits in software development?

output:
Code refactoring is the process of restructuring existing code without changing its external behavior. The goal of refactoring is to improve the code's readability, maintainability, and overall quality. 
In the given Java code, there is not much room for refactoring as it is a very simple program. However, we can still make some minor changes to improve its readability and maintainability. One possible refactoring technique that can be applied to this code is to extract the string "Hello, World!" into a separate variable. This can be done as follows:
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String message = "Hello, World!";
        System.out.println(message);
    }
}
